  "$comment": "Files and routes that use the Mindy public design system. scripts/audit-public-design.mjs lints every entry in `files` (directories are walked). scripts/verify-public-site.mjs runs runtime checks on `runtimeRoutes`; scripts/verify-public-parity.mjs diffs raw HTML for `parityRoutes`. A route migration adds its owning files and routes here in the same PR. The homepage is listed as /today: getmindy.ai/ rewrites there by host, so on localhost / is a different page. MeetMindyStrip, MemberAwareCta and ShareButton are also rendered by routes not yet migrated (/top, /shared/opp, /weird, /up-for-grabs); they carry an appearance prop and are verified here at runtime, not linted, until those routes migrate. PR 3 adds the raw-HTML families (/gov, /institute, /pilot, /research, the Observatory report, /bid), which reach the system through src/lib/public-site/html.ts, usually via the family shell src/lib/gov/shell.ts; and the public /mcp pages. /mcp/account is the signed-in console and stays on its own theme, as does src/app/mcp/catalog-ui.tsx, which it shares. /partners is a 308 to /gov/apex and has no page of its own. /gov/market-research is a separate signed-out tool demo that does not use the gov shell; it is not part of PR 3. PR 4 adds the ProductPageAppSumo family (13 source pages; 5 of them, like the three /bundles pages, redirect in production, so those are parity-checked on status + Location only and linted, not rendered), the /top family, /up-for-grabs, /weird, /shared/opp, and the legacy marketing pages. Intentionally non-migrated public routes and their reasons: docs/design/public-site/NOT-MIGRATED.md. `redirectRoutes` are source files that production redirects (host-conditional rules in next.config.ts, or a redirect in the page): verify-public-parity fetches them with the production Host and compares status + Location only.",
